<!--
  US-175: build.gradle.kts sets `baseline = file("lint-baseline.xml")` with
  abortOnError = true, but this file did not exist. When the baseline is
  missing, the Android Gradle Plugin creates it and then *fails* the build to
  report that it did — so the very first CI lint invocation failed by design,
  every time.

  This baseline is intentionally empty: it suppresses nothing, so lint reports
  every issue it finds and abortOnError stays a real gate. It exists only to
  remove the bootstrap failure.

  If CI surfaces pre-existing error-severity issues, fix them rather than
  baselining them. To record genuinely deferred issues, run
  `./gradlew updateLintBaseline` and commit the regenerated file.
-->
